commit 7852470aff5b35087bf537bf1137dd4fb3ab1451
Author: Kenneth Jiang <kenneth.jiang@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Oct 14 15:11:32 2026 -0700

    Printer flows drop or keep unsaved edits instead of refusing

    Three printer paths still refused, or raised Orca's prompt, when the
    project's printer had unsaved edits. They now follow the same rule as
    project_open and printer_setup: no prompt, and nothing is lost for good.

    A nozzle change rewrites the saved profile and the project's copy follows
    it, dropping the unsaved edits; printer_change lists their keys in
    discarded. The printer panel's coordinator now saves a version before
    printer_change, as the project's agent pane does for any change to the
    project, so the dropped edits stay in history. A shell harness check
    restores that version and finds the edit; it fails without the hook.

    Connecting writes the three connection settings into the saved profile
    and the project's copy; its other unsaved edits stay. Renaming no longer
    calls Orca's save-or-discard prompt: the edits are set aside and loaded
    again, still unsaved, on the printer they belong to.

    15 files, 122 lines added, 77 removed.

